id: absorb
name: Absorb
type: standard
actionCost: 2
kiCost: 0
attacking: false
requiresTarget: true
special: true
usageLimit: 2/round
# Folded, because `coerce` splits a header value on commas and this line has one in it.
exploitable: >
  If you fail the initial Clash, this triggers the Exploit Maneuver from the target.
exploitOnLoss: true
source: Core Rule
description: >
  A Clash (Strike vs Strike/Dodge) at a Character in your Melee Range, then one (Corporeal): won, they are removed from the Combat
  Encounter and you gain a stack of the Absorption Awakening; lost, they are Shaken.
text: >
  Absorb Maneuver [2/Round]: You consume, wrap around, or otherwise engulf a target and make them part of yourself.
  –Maneuver Type: Standard Maneuver
  –Action Cost: 2 Actions
  –Minions: Non-Minion
  –KP Cost: N/A
  –Exploitable: If you fail the initial Clash, this triggers the Exploit Maneuver from the target.
  –Effect: Target a Character within your Melee Range. Make a Clash (Strike vs Strike/Dodge) against them. If you win, make a
  second Clash (Corporeal) against that Character. If you lose this Clash, that Character suffers from the Shaken Combat Condition
  until the end of their next turn. If you win, that Character is removed from the Combat Encounter and you gain a stack of the
  Absorption Awakening as a Level 2 Temporary Awakening with that Character as the Absorbed Character.

---

# A Special Maneuver: nobody's until an effect gives it (Assimilation (2), Natural Dragon in the Ball Form).
#
# Asked before anything is paid (use-maneuver.mjs): not a Minion yourself ("Minions: Non-Minion" - the Biography's box), a Character
# targeted within your Melee Range. Then (chat.mjs postAbsorbClash, settleAbsorb): the Clash, Strike against their Strike or Dodge -
# lost, their Exploit offered on its card (`exploitOnLoss`); won, the Clash (Corporeal). That one lost: Shaken till the end of their
# next turn. Won: out of the Combat Encounter - Combatant gone, token hidden, by the GM - and a stack of the Absorption Awakening, its
# mark, naming the Absorbed Character (flags absorbedWith).
#
# Not built: Awakenings are not in this system - the Absorption Awakening's own effects, and what "Temporary" makes of it, are the
# table's; the stack is what is kept.
